@* AlertStatesGallery.razor — states gallery for comparing AppAlert's two
   severities against the Figma reference (TaskTwo_from_figma_design.png).
   Same convention as ActionBannerStatesGallery.razor/StepperStatesGallery.razor
   — not part of Screen A/B, uses only the shared AppAlert + shared tokens/
   CSS, no page-specific component styling (the <style> block below is
   layout-only, per CLAUDE.md §3). *@
@page "/demo/alert-states"

<PageTitle>AppAlert — states gallery</PageTitle>

<h1>AppAlert — states gallery</h1>
<p>
    Both severities confirmed against
    <code>demo/ScreenB/TaskTwo_from_figma_design.png</code>: a content-sized,
    unbordered, fully-rounded pill per severity (see AppAlert.razor's own
    header comment for the pixel verification). Warning uses
    <code>role="alert"</code>; Success uses <code>role="status"</code>.
</p>

<div class="alert-states-grid">
    <div class="alert-states-cell">
        <h2>Warning — role="alert"</h2>
        <AppAlert Severity="AppAlertSeverity.Warning"
                  Message="إجراء مطلوب: يرجى التأكد من وجود قسم واحد على الأقل، وأن جميع الأسئلة موزعة بالكامل" />
    </div>

    <div class="alert-states-cell">
        <h2>Success — role="status"</h2>
        <AppAlert Severity="AppAlertSeverity.Success"
                  Message="اخترت عدة أسئلة باستخدام مربعات الاختيارات، ثم قم بتعيينها لدفعة واحدة" />
    </div>
</div>

<style>
    /* Page-local layout only (stacked arrangement of the gallery itself) —
       not a reusable visual pattern, so it's fine here rather than
       components.css per CLAUDE.md §3.1's rule of thumb. Nothing here sets
       a color/size that AppAlert itself needs. */
    .alert-states-grid {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 24px;
        max-width: 700px;
    }

    .alert-states-cell h2 {
        font-size: 14px;
        margin: 0 0 8px;
    }
</style>
